  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 202 AM CDT Sat Aug 1 2026\n\nRidging attempts to build over the Desert Southwest again by the \nbeginning of the Long Term period. This allows highs to once again \njump into the upper 90s and just above 100 degrees for many \nlocations Monday and Tuesday. However, guidance indicates the ridge \nwill be more broad and generally not as potent as we saw last week, \nthanks in part to shortwaves moving across northern portions of the \nCONUS. Additionally, we look to remain on the eastern periphery of \nthe ridge. As a result, temperatures look less hot overall than what \nwe experienced during the latter portion of July. By the middle part \nof next week and through the end of the forecast period, highs tick \ndown a degree or two relative to Monday and Tuesday, remaining \nconsistently in the upper 90s for most locations. Rain chances \nthrough the Long Term look very low at this time (<20%).\n\nSprang",
